Z||000000||Pheagey||11-07-2001||10:41 AM||||  I had a nice running '88 coupe till vandals got ahold of it.<BR>  If I got a junk yard and pick up another column would I have to get another outta a manual (my coupe is a manual) and how much should I pay for one?<BR>  (also if anyone has 4 stock rimms w/ tires on them (any condition) lemme know).<P>------------------<BR>"There is no replacement for displacement.Period"<BR>    -Mr.Frosty<P>'88 coupe, 5 speed: Status: Unknown.<BR>Broken down: 3 times<BR>Broken into: 2  times (w/i 2 days)<BR>Killed: '97 Civic LX Auto,<BR>Killed by: '93 Civic EX 5 speed,<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects.com/car.html||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||11-07-2001||10:44 AM||||For the wheels, call Don Hulse. 770-949-8648. Before 10:00 PM. <BR>I think he's got a set, with nearly new tires. I doubt he'll be able to ship them, though. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pheagey||11-07-2001||11:19 AM||||forgot to ask how much time and h=how hard it is to swap the columns...||||reg||5
Z||000003||fix||11-07-2001||11:36 AM||||no, you shouldn't need a column out of a manual car.  An automatic will work too, but you will have to be sure to disable the park/neutral safety switch on an automatic steering column.  It's just a mechanical safety switch that keeps you from turning the key unless the car is in park or neutral.  If you remove the column you shouldn't have any trouble figuring out the switch.  Removal of the steering column itself is not very difficult.  I would imagine that even having never done it before you could have it out in at less than an hour. I'm not sure how much they're going for, so I guess I would just call around until you find the best deal. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||JD86GT350||11-07-2001||06:30 PM||||not sure if the '88 is different, but I swapped an '84 auto tilt and an '86 stick straight column with each other.  I'd never done it before, and had I not bumped the clutch neutral start switch I could have had both columns out and back into the other cars in an hour....but I got a little distracted.  The swap was very easy.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodrv6||11-07-2001||06:39 PM||||88 columns are the same as all the others, so it should be fairly easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
